+// the usual AES-encrypted `data` field most zca-js API responses use.
+// `utils.resolve()` defaults to `isEncrypted = true`, which tried to
+// AES-decrypt the literal number `1` and, because crypto-js silently
+// returns an empty string on bad ciphertext/padding rather than throwing,
+// produced "Failed to parse response data: SyntaxError: Unexpected end of
+// JSON input" (from `JSON.parse("")`) even though the call had already
+// succeeded server-side. Fixed by passing `isEncrypted = false` to
+// `utils.resolve()` here so `result.data` is used as-is.
+//
+// (Earlier iterations of this file also had a real bug where
+// `utils.resolve(response)` was called without `await` — since it wraps
+// an `async function`, that returned a pending Promise instead of the
+// actual result, which silently broke a since-removed multi-candidate
+// fallback loop. Not relevant now that the domain is confirmed and this
+// is back to a single direct call, but noted here in case this file ever
+// grows a retry/fallback again: always `await utils.resolve(...)`.)
